Chapter: GlyphsOnScreen
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Encode chapter TrueType
  cites Ui chapter GlyphRasterizer
  cites Works chapter GopDraw

 The small TrueType font codex/test/truetype-render-test embeds, parsed by
 TrueType and its letter A rasterized by GlyphRasterizer at 16, 24 and 32
 pixels to the em, onto the screen that UEFI's GOP protocol describes with each
 glyph pixel a 3 by 3 block: plain coverage along the top row, and the
 anti-aliased render, its coverage as grey, along the bottom.

 We say:

Section: Screen

  fb-base : Integer = 3204448256
  cell-width : Integer = 1988
  cell-height : Integer = 1992
  cell-stride : Integer = 2016

  paper : Integer = #1B1F2A
  chalk : Integer = #F4F1E8

Section: Font

 truetype-render-test's font, byte for byte: a cmap, a glyph table holding a
